// Both lanes' composed identity: Deep runs `advocate` and Echo runs `admin-assist`. The
// role named below is the template's only, rewritten per role by
// scripts/stage-compose-sources.sh, and `SIRENS_ECHO_ROLE` picks which baked
// bundle a deployment loads. This file is composed once per role at build time.
//
// It carries no `identity` node for the same reason: one template bakes every
// roster role, so a seat name here would rename all of them. The stage script
// injects one per role, and only ops has one, because only Echo brings its own
// identity. See docs/sirens-echo-identity.md.
//
// Every source uses `declaration=`, never `root=`. With `root=` the source
// repository's own .agents/roles.kdl decides, and agentic-os-kai's roles
// deliberately bind Kai's career, job-search, and LinkedIn context because
// they serve Kai rather than a public Discord agent. That binding is also what
// makes `ops` safe here: agentic-os-kai binds infrastructure, deploy, and
// hardware to that role, and a declaration admits none of it, so Echo composes
// the operator charter without the estate. See docs/sirens-echo-compose.md.
compose {
    role "creator"
    delivery "native-skills"
    source "aos-public" declaration="aos-public.kdl" required=#true
}
